{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","index":0,"message":{"content":"I have a strong lead. Let me reconsider the structure carefully:\n\n- Award created in 2000s → International Booker Prize (established 2005)\n- Book A: contender for this award, translated into 25+ languages, published in the 2010s\n- In the year Book A was published, Book B won the award\n- Book B was released the preceding year\n- Author of Book B born in city where author of Book A grew up\n\nKey candidate: Chigozie Obioma's \"An Orchestra of Minorities\" (2019) was shortlisted for the Booker Prize and translated into 30 languages. But wait — that's the Booker Prize, not the International Booker Prize. Let me reconsider.\n\nActually, the question says \"the very award above for which the first book was later in contention.\" So Book A is a contender for the award, and Book B won that same award. Let me check the International Booker Prize winners in the 2010s and look for the connection. Let me search for the Wikipedia page on the International Booker Prize.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"International Booker Prize Wikipedia\", \"Booker International Prize 2016 2017 2018 2019 winner\", \"Man Booker International Prize Wikipedia\"], \"top_k\": 8}","name":"search"},"id":"call_d20bb2a0245c40d5b8029639","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Chigozie Obioma biography born Akure grew up\", \"Chigozie Obioma Wikipedia\", \"An Orchestra of Minorities 2019 Booker shortlist\"], \"top_k\": 8}","name":"search"},"id":"call_0b955f4df9c349549d6718ff","index":1,"type":"function"}]}}],"created":1789490057,"id":"chatcmpl-569e70f3-ccc9-9f90-8a00-5d921b4df72b","model":"glm-5.2","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"prompt_tokens":16626,"completion_tokens":319,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":16945,"cached_tokens":3584,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":3584},"prompt_cost":0.000000,"completion_cost":0.000000,"cache_cost":0.0